 hw/timer/mchp_tcc.c                           | 523 +++++++++++++++++-
 include/hw/mchp/gen/atsame51j20a/tcc_u2213.h  |   7 +-
 .../mchp/gen/pic32cm1216mc00048/tcc_u2213.h   |   7 +-
 .../mchp/gen/pic32cm5164jh01100/tcc_u2213.h   |   7 +-
 include/hw/mchp/gen/tcc_u2213.h               |   2 +-
 include/hw/timer/mchp_tcc.h                   |   3 +
 tests/qtest/pic32cm-tcc-test.c                | 255 ++++++++-
 8 files changed, 776 insertions(+), 40 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-jh01-cpro.rst b/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-jh01-cpro.rst
index 1a1dd3b..3d337eb 100644
--- a/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-jh01-cpro.rst
+++ b/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-jh01-cpro.rst
@@ -107,7 +107,11 @@ Supported devices
   an instance lacks keep their bits at zero, and WAVE and PATT drop a
   write made while the previous one synchronizes. STOP and the end of a
   one-shot put each output at DRVCTRL.NRVx where NREx is set and leave
-  the others floating.
+  the others floating. Recoverable faults A and B (the MC0/MC1 event
+  inputs) clamp their channel, with filter, blanking, qualification,
+  keep, restart, hardware and software halt and capture into a CPTENx
+  channel; non-recoverable faults (EV0/EV1, or HALT = NR) hold the
+  counter in the DRVCTRL state until software clears them.
 - RTC (U2250, PIC32CM MC00 only): the three modes, periodic flags,
   calendar with alarm, event outputs; reset only at power-on.
 - EVSYS: channels on the three paths, software events, the users that
@@ -160,8 +164,10 @@ Missing devices
   timeouts and 10-bit/high-speed I2C addressing, the USART external clock
   (XCK), synchronous mode, LIN and auto-baud frames, IrDA, 9-bit characters
   and receive errors. PORT: the sampling mode (CTRL).
-- TC capture on pins (COPEN) and CAPTMODE; the JH01 RTC (03608). TCC faults,
-  capture, circular buffers, RAMP2CS and the outputs' start latency.
+- TC capture on pins (COPEN) and CAPTMODE; the JH01 RTC (03608). TCC
+  capture from events, the fault capture modes but CAPT, the ALTFAULT
+  source, circular buffers, RAMP2CS, the outputs' start latency and the
+  STATUS read lag.
 - PAC write protection, DSU CRC32 and chip erase, sleep modes and every other
   peripheral behaviour (CCL, PDEC, CAN, ...). ADC
   sequencing and event inputs, DAC START events.
